[]    2) When people say `low levels', how far down are you referring to?

tricky semantics here. a low level character would be one with little
experience (i.e. a small number for an experience stat). so a low
dungeon level could be expected to mean a dungeon level with a small
number but probably actually means a _deep_ dungeon level. let's say
that hell typically starts at level 30. a deep level would then be,
let's say level 25 (around Medusa) and a deep hell level might be 45,
or so. btw, things change slightly in going from pl6 to pl7 and the
game is now at_ pl9_ (not a typo folks, get your new binaries soon,
when they are announced).

[]    3) I have noticed that a lot of mention has been made of wishing and
[]    altars, and in my travels i have been lucky enuf to find but a few
[]    altars and no wands of wishing.

altars are sometimes frustatingly rare. in fact, it is possible to go a
whole game and not find one until the last moment (i think), but that
isn't common. it is more likely that you'll find an altar every few
levels or so (and it need not be a co-aligned altar to be useful).

wands of wishing are extremely rare! however there is at least one wand
of wishing to be found in every game (talk to the oracle). naturally,
one would expect that such a powerful thing would be heavily guarded.

